WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.340
In autumn, many Virginia trees drop their leaves onto the forest floor.

2
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.720
Leaves fall every year.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.320
If nothing happened to them, the layers would stack higher and higher.

4
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.040
So where do all the fallen leaves go?

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.000
What would happen if nothing broke them down?

6
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:25.893
Every living thing in a forest does one of three jobs.

7
00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:32.073
A producer captures energy from sunlight and stores it in sugar, also called

8
00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:36.853
glucose. Trees, grasses and mosses are producers.

9
00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:41.693
A consumer gets energy by eating other organisms.

10
00:00:42.813 --> 00:00:45.053
A deer eating acorns is a consumer.

11
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:51.097
A decomposer breaks down dead plants, dead animals and wastes.

12
00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:54.937
The main decomposers are fungi and bacteria.

13
00:00:56.057 --> 00:00:57.717
A fungus has no mouth.

14
00:00:58.297 --> 00:01:02.437
It releases chemicals that break down the leaf outside its body.

15
00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.297
Then it takes in the small pieces.

16
00:01:06.457 --> 00:01:10.917
Worms and millipedes help by tearing dead leaves into smaller bits.

17
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.340
As decomposers break down a leaf, nutrients go back into the soil.

18
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.380
A nutrient is a substance, such as nitrogen, that living things need to grow.

19
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.700
Plant roots take up those nutrients and use them again.

20
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:34.840
Some of the leaf's carbon goes into the air as carbon dioxide, released by decomposers.

21
00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:38.033
Now take the decomposers away.

22
00:01:39.013 --> 00:01:40.773
Dead leaves would pile up.

23
00:01:41.293 --> 00:01:46.533
Fewer nutrients would return to the soil, so plants may grow less over time.

24
00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:51.413
Producers, consumers and decomposers are linked.

25
00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:54.933
A change in one group reaches the others.

26
00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:58.417
Matter goes around and around.

27
00:01:59.297 --> 00:02:04.277
Energy does not. Energy enters as sunlight and leaves as heat.

28
00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:06.877
So where do the fallen leaves go?

29
00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:13.577
Fungi, bacteria and small animals break them down, and the nutrients go back into

30
00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:15.777
the soil, where trees take them up again.
